.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OPENSSL-KDF 1ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openssl-kdf
.Nd perform Key Derivation Function operations
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm openssl kdf
.Oo
.Fl help ]
.Oo
.Fl cipher ]
.Oo
.Fl digest ]
.Oo
.Fl mac ]
.Oo
.Fl kdfopt
.Em nm Ns : Ns Em v ]
.Oo
.Fl keylen
.Em num ]
.Oo
.Fl out
.Em filename ]
.Oo
.Fl binary ]
.Oo
.Fl provider
.Em name ]
.Oo
.Fl provider-path
.Em path ]
.Oo
.Fl provparam
.Em [name:]key=value ]
.Oo
.Fl propquery
.Em propq ]
.Em kdf_name
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The key derivation functions generate a derived key from either a secret
or password.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy -help
Print a usage message.
.It Sy -keylen Em num
The output size of the derived key.
This field is required.
.It Sy -out Em filename
Filename to output to, or standard output by default.
.It Sy -binary
Output the derived key in binary form.
Uses hexadecimal text format if not specified.
.It Sy -cipher Em name
Specify the cipher to be used by the KDF. Not all KDFs require a cipher
and it is an error to use this option in such cases.
.It Sy -digest Em name
Specify the digest to be used by the KDF. Not all KDFs require a digest
and it is an error to use this option in such cases.
To see the list of supported digests, use
.Qo Li openssl list -digest-commands Qc .
.It Sy -mac Em name
Specify the MAC to be used by the KDF. Not all KDFs require a MAC and it
is an error to use this option in such cases.
.It Sy -kdfopt Em nm Ns : Ns Em v
Passes options to the KDF algorithm.
A comprehensive list of parameters can be found in
.Xr EVP_KDF 3 .
Common parameter names used by
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_set_params 3
are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy key: Ns Em string
Specifies the secret key as an alphanumeric string (use if the key
contains printable characters only).
The string length must conform to any restrictions of the KDF algorithm.
A key must be specified for most KDF algorithms.
.It Sy hexkey: Ns Em string
Alternative to the
.Sy key:
option where the secret key is specified in hexadecimal form (two hex
digits per byte).
.It Sy pass: Ns Em string
Specifies the password as an alphanumeric string (use if the password
contains printable characters only).
The password must be specified for PBKDF2 and scrypt.
.It Sy hexpass: Ns Em string
Alternative to the
.Sy pass:
option where the password is specified in hexadecimal form (two hex
digits per byte).
.It Sy salt: Ns Em string
Specifies a non-secret unique cryptographic salt as an alphanumeric
string (use if it contains printable characters only).
The length must conform to any restrictions of the KDF algorithm.
A salt parameter is required for several KDF algorithms, such as
.Xr EVP_KDF-PBKDF2 7 .
.It Sy hexsalt: Ns Em string
Alternative to the
.Sy salt:
option where the salt is specified in hexadecimal form (two hex digits
per byte).
.It Sy info: Ns Em string
Some KDF implementations, such as
.Xr EVP_KDF-HKDF 7 ,
take an 'info' parameter for binding the derived key material to
application- and context-specific information.
Specifies the info, fixed info, other info or shared info argument as an
alphanumeric string (use if it contains printable characters only).
The length must conform to any restrictions of the KDF algorithm.
.It Sy hexinfo: Ns Em string
Alternative to the
.Sy info:
option where the info is specified in hexadecimal form (two hex digits
per byte).
.It Sy digest: Ns Em string
This option is identical to the
.Sy -digest
option.
.It Sy cipher: Ns Em string
This option is identical to the
.Sy -cipher
option.
.It Sy mac: Ns Em string
This option is identical to the
.Sy -mac
option.
.El
.It Sy -provider Em name
.It Sy -provider-path Em path
.It Sy -provparam Em [name:]key=value
.It Sy -propquery Em propq
See
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
and
.Xr property 7 .
.It Em kdf_name
Specifies the name of a supported KDF algorithm which will be used.
The supported algorithms names include TLS1-PRF, HKDF, SSKDF, PBKDF2,
SSHKDF, X942KDF-ASN1, X942KDF-CONCAT, X963KDF and SCRYPT.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Use TLS1-PRF to create a hex-encoded derived key from a secret key and
seed:
.Bd -literal
    openssl kdf -keylen 16 -kdfopt digest:SHA2-256 -kdfopt key:secret \e
                -kdfopt seed:seed TLS1-PRF
.Ed
.Pp
Use HKDF to create a hex-encoded derived key from a secret key, salt and
info:
.Bd -literal
    openssl kdf -keylen 10 -kdfopt digest:SHA2-256 -kdfopt key:secret \e
                -kdfopt salt:salt -kdfopt info:label HKDF
.Ed
.Pp
Use SSKDF with KMAC to create a hex-encoded derived key from a secret
key, salt and info:
.Bd -literal
    openssl kdf -keylen 64 -kdfopt mac:KMAC-128 -kdfopt maclen:20 \e
                -kdfopt hexkey:b74a149a161545 -kdfopt hexinfo:348a37a2 \e
                -kdfopt hexsalt:3638271ccd68a2 SSKDF
.Ed
.Pp
Use SSKDF with HMAC to create a hex-encoded derived key from a secret
key, salt and info:
.Bd -literal
    openssl kdf -keylen 16 -kdfopt mac:HMAC -kdfopt digest:SHA2-256 \e
                -kdfopt hexkey:b74a149a -kdfopt hexinfo:348a37a2 \e
                -kdfopt hexsalt:3638271c SSKDF
.Ed
.Pp
Use SSKDF with Hash to create a hex-encoded derived key from a secret
key, salt and info:
.Bd -literal
    openssl kdf -keylen 14 -kdfopt digest:SHA2-256 \e
                -kdfopt hexkey:6dbdc23f045488 \e
                -kdfopt hexinfo:a1b2c3d4 SSKDF
.Ed
.Pp
Use SSHKDF to create a hex-encoded derived key from a secret key, hash
and session_id:
.Bd -literal
    openssl kdf -keylen 16 -kdfopt digest:SHA2-256 \e
                -kdfopt hexkey:0102030405 \e
                -kdfopt hexxcghash:06090A \e
                -kdfopt hexsession_id:01020304 \e
                -kdfopt type:A SSHKDF
.Ed
.Pp
Use PBKDF2 to create a hex-encoded derived key from a password and salt:
.Bd -literal
    openssl kdf -keylen 32 -kdfopt digest:SHA256 -kdfopt pass:password \e
                -kdfopt salt:salt -kdfopt iter:2 PBKDF2
.Ed
.Pp
Use scrypt to create a hex-encoded derived key from a password and salt:
.Bd -literal
    openssl kdf -keylen 64 -kdfopt pass:password -kdfopt salt:NaCl \e
                -kdfopt n:1024 -kdfopt r:8 -kdfopt p:16 \e
                -kdfopt maxmem_bytes:10485760 SCRYPT
.Ed
.Sh NOTES
The KDF mechanisms that are available will depend on the options used
when building OpenSSL.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr openssl-pkeyutl 1 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF-SCRYPT 7 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF-TLS1_PRF 7 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF-PBKDF2 7 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF-HKDF 7 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF-SS 7 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF-SSHKDF 7 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF-X942-ASN1 7 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF-X942-CONCAT 7 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF-X963 7
